course: dictionary
lesson: 1834
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Cob is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context and they give clues. «Each silk thread on a maize cob is joined to one kernel» tells you that a cob is part of a plant, because maize is a kind of corn and kernels are its seeds.
explain: «Count the rows on a cob and you nearly always get an even number.» Here cob must mean the part of corn that the kernels grow on, since you count rows of kernels. Always ask: which meaning fits here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Other clues can point to a different meaning. Near water, feathers, or a lake, cob probably means a male swan. Near a farm, a cart, or a field, it may mean a horse. When the clues do not settle it, a dictionary will tell you the exact meaning.
fact: A cob is the long middle part of an ear of corn, the part the kernels grow on.
fact: «Corn on the cob» means sweetcorn cooked whole, with the kernels still on the cob.
fact: A cob is a male swan. A female swan is a pen, and a baby swan is a cygnet.
fact: A cob is a small round loaf of bread, or a bread roll in some parts of England. A cob is also a strong, short-legged horse.
fact: Cob is also a mix of clay, straw and water, used to build the thick walls of old houses, such as cob cottages in Devon.
exercise: «Count the rows on a cob and you nearly always get an even number.» What is a cob in this sentence? | *The middle part of an ear of corn | A bread roll | A male swan | A strong horse
exercise: The farmer's cob pulled the heavy cart up the hill. What is a cob here? | *A strong, short-legged horse | A bread roll | Clay mixed with straw | A male swan
exercise: What does «corn on the cob» mean? | Corn stored in a sack | Corn ground into flour | *Sweetcorn cooked whole | A cornfield in winter
test: «The cob glided across the lake, and the pen followed with her cygnets.» What is a cob in this sentence? | A strong horse | *A male swan | A baby swan | A female swan
test: In a history lesson, the thick walls of an old Devon cottage were made of cob. What is cob? | A loaf of bread | A kind of corn | A swan's nest | *A mix of clay, straw and water
exam: «Each silk thread on a maize cob is joined to one kernel.» What does cob mean in this sentence? | A mix of clay and straw | *The long middle part of an ear of corn | A male swan | A small round loaf
